-- title:
--   Rank certificate for mask 97
-- statement:
--   Let $r(m)$ be the specified rank table for the mask of unit residues modulo 30, and let $s_g(m)$ be the specified subproduct-mask update by a residue code $g\in C_2\times C_4$. For the fixed mask $m=97$,
--
--   $$r(m)\le5,\qquad r(m)=5\iff (0,0)\in\operatorname{supp}(m),\qquad \forall g,\ \min(r(m)+1,5)\le r(s_g(m)).$$
--
--   Here mask support uses the eight-bit residue ordering $1,7,11,13,17,19,23,29$, and $(0,0)$ is the code of residue one. This is one finite certificate row; no assertion for other masks is made by this row alone.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, Certified minimal memory for a divisor-residue presence observable modulo 30, https://zenodo.org/records/23989640; archive Couret_BC_MOD30_Companion_20261105.zip, SHA-256 9bb2678164c63a9e47c192093f5ce9deb1b7b74a1f1c8fecc77f305a408266a2; file source/S5/RankBlock06.lean, lines 8–8; source file SHA-256 c75ce1af5a79a87826d359821ecfd18a5d6efd224a4153bb7e6ecf43476d435d; theorem Couret.S5.rank_row_97

